  "notes": {
    "heritage": "The 2JZ-GTE is widely considered one of the greatest engines ever produced. Developed as part of Toyota's JZ engine family, it represents the pinnacle of Toyota's inline-6 turbo engineering. The iron block design allows for extreme boost levels while maintaining reliability.",
    "reputation": "LEGENDARY status in the tuning world. Stock internals have been proven to handle 800+ HP reliably. With basic bolt-ons, 500HP is easily achievable. World record builds have exceeded 2000HP on the factory block. The closed-deck design and oil squirters contribute to its unmatched durability.",
    "common_issues": [
      "Timing belt failure (replace every 60k miles)",
      "Stock turbo ceramic wheels can shatter at high boost",
      "Sequential turbo system complexity (transition valve issues)",
      "Oil leaks from cam seals and valve covers",
      "Crank position sensor failure",
      "Throttle position sensor wear",
      "IACV (Idle Air Control Valve) failure",
      "Water pump weep hole leak"
    ],
    "strengths": [
      "Incredibly strong iron block - handles 1000+ HP on stock internals",
      "Forged crankshaft from factory",
      "Oil squirters for piston cooling",
      "Closed deck design for cylinder rigidity",
      "Large displacement (3.0L) provides excellent torque",
      "Smooth inline-6 power delivery",
      "Massive aftermarket support worldwide",
      "Engine design allows for enormous turbo upgrades",
      "Head flows well for factory casting",
      "Simple distributor-less ignition system"
    ],
    "maintenance_critical": [
      "Timing belt and tensioner every 60,000 miles",
      "Water pump replacement with timing belt",
      "Cam seals inspection during timing belt service",
      "Valve cover gaskets every 80,000 miles",
      "Spark plugs every 30,000 miles",
      "Oil changes every 3,000-5,000 miles with quality oil"
    ],
    "historical_significance": "The 2JZ-GTE became a cultural icon through the Fast & Furious franchise and 1990s import tuning scene. Its combination of Toyota reliability, massive power potential, and smooth inline-6 character made it the benchmark for all sport compact engines. Even 25+ years after production ended, it remains the gold standard for engine swaps."
